  "body": "Signed-off-by: Zach Aller <zach_aller@intuit.com>\n",
  "references": [
    {
      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-02T11:27:47-05:00",
        "subject": "fix(ui): link commits on GitLab and Bitbucket Cloud correctly (#2282)",
        "body": "Every commit link in the Promotion Explorer was built as\n<repo>/commit/<sha>. That works for GitHub, Gitea, Forgejo, and Azure\nDevOps, and Bitbucket Data Center was already special-cased by URL\nshape, but GitLab serves commits at /-/commit/<sha> and Bitbucket Cloud\nat /commits/<sha>, so those links were broken.\n\nThe PromotionStrategyDetails bundle from the dashboard APIService now\ncarries the strategy's ScmProvider or ClusterScmProvider. The dashboard\nand the Argo CD extension pass its spec to the explorer, and\ngetCommitUrl uses the GitLab or Bitbucket Cloud layout for URLs on that\nprovider's domain. That covers self-hosted GitLab and Bitbucket Cloud\ndomain overrides, which a hard-coded host list can't. gitlab.com and\nbitbucket.org are recognized without the provider, so references to\ncommits on those hosts from other repos link correctly too.\n\nThe dashboard store keeps the provider specs beside its items rather\nthan on them, since the live manifest view renders the item as the\nPromotionStrategy.\n\nSupersedes the domain lookup in #1037.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Mp42qe21Ft6tLnS2TnGysd\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "390ace2ddcd11d2a8d24c8480ea3339400530366",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
